DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The eeppiicc interface provides access to the 10Mb/s and 100Mb/s Ethernet
     networks via the SMC EPIC chipset.  This driver provides support for the
     SMC EtherPower II 10/100 Ethernet cards.

     The eeppiicc supports several media types, which are selected via the
     ifconfig(8) command.  The supported media types are:

           mmeeddiiaa autoselect
                   Attempt to autoselect the media type (default)

           mmeeddiiaa 100baseFX mmeeddiiaaoopptt full-duplex
                   Use 100baseFX (fiber), full duplex

           mmeeddiiaa 100baseFX mmeeddiiaaoopptt half-duplex
                   Use 100baseFX (fiber), half duplex

           mmeeddiiaa 100baseTX mmeeddiiaaoopptt full-duplex
                   Use 100baseTX, full duplex

           mmeeddiiaa 100baseTX mmeeddiiaaoopptt half-duplex
                   Use 100baseTX, half duplex

           mmeeddiiaa 100baseTX mmeeddiiaaoopptt loopback
                   Put the interface into loopback mode

           mmeeddiiaa 10baseT mmeeddiiaaoopptt full-duplex
                   Use 10baseT, full duplex

           mmeeddiiaa 10baseT mmeeddiiaaoopptt half-duplex
                   Use 10baseT, half duplex

           mmeeddiiaa 10baseT mmeeddiiaaoopptt loopback
                   Put the interface into loopback mode

